UPDATE companies SET description='Falcon Plastics was founded in 1975 in Brookings, South Dakota, as a family-owned custom plastics molder. From its start molding customer ideas into quality plastic products, the company has grown into a multi-facility operation with plants in South Dakota, Oregon, and Tennessee, supplemented by strategic manufacturing partnerships in Mexico and Asia.

The company specializes in mid-to-high volume custom injection molding, blow molding, tool and mold making, sheet foaming (EVA), and foam-in-place gasketing. Its facilities include temperature-controlled white rooms with HEPA filtration for clean molding, and smart work cells equipped with process monitoring, automated in-line quality testing, and robotic acceptance or rejection systems. Value-added assembly and lean manufacturing principles support cost-effective volume production.

Falcon serves medical device, electronics, consumer product, automotive, business machine, construction, and recreation/sports markets. Customers rely on the molder for precision components that meet strict regulatory standards in medical applications, durable housings for electronics, and high-performance parts for automotive and industrial uses.

The company emphasizes a multi-facility model that provides supply-chain flexibility without sacrificing control or quality. Its stated differentiators include reducing cycle times, optimizing material usage, and maintaining an ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system across all sites, driven by a culture of continuous improvement and on-time delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom injection molding", "Custom blow molding", "Tool and mold making", "Sheet foaming (EVA)", "Foam-in-place gasketing", "Value-added assembly", "Quality assurance", "Clean room molding (white rooms)", "Automated in-line quality testing", "Robotic part acceptance/rejection", "Process monitoring", "Lean manufacturing"], "industries": ["Medical Devices", "Electronics", "Consumer Products", "Automotive", "Business Machines", "Construction", "Recreation/Sports"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["HEPA air filtration systems", "Robotic acceptance/rejection systems", "Process monitoring systems", "Automated in-line quality test systems"], "volume": "Mid-to-high volume", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Multi-facility model with U.S., Mexico, and Asia production", "White rooms with HEPA filtration for clean molding", "Smart work cells with process monitoring and automated in-line quality testing", "Lean manufacturing principles applied to injection molding", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system across all facilities"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1975 -> /about", "Family-owned -> /", "Headquarters in Brookings, South Dakota -> db", "Facilities in South Dakota, Oregon, Tennessee -> /quality", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "Capabilities: injection molding, blow molding, tool and mold making, sheet foaming EVA, foam-in-place gasketing -> /", "Industries: medical devices, electronics, consumer products, automotive, business machines, construction, recreation/sports -> /, /capabilities", "White rooms with HEPA filtration -> /capabilities", "Smart work cells with process monitoring and automated in-line quality tests -> /", "Robotic acceptance/rejection systems -> /", "Lean manufacturing principles -> /", "Multi-facility model with Mexico and Asia -> /", "Mid-to-high volume -> /about", "Quality policy continuous improvement -> /quality"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Falcon Plastics has become a mid-to-high volume custom plastic molder of choice with the vision and capacity to engineer, manufacture, assemble, and distribute product", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='falcon-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Falls Millwork has operated from Kelley, Iowa, since 1990. The business was built around master craftsman Ben Svec, who brought more than 40 years of woodworking experience to the venture.

The company produces a wide range of custom wood products, including cabinetry, reproduction moldings, entry doors, specialty windows, staircases, built-ins, fireplace mantels, and liturgical furniture. Its shop handles vacuum-formed curved components, hardware integration, and trial assembly before installation. Projects span full interior remodels to single furnishing pieces.

Customers include homeowners seeking custom interiors for kitchens, bathrooms, and bedrooms; commercial clients needing architectural millwork for public spaces; and religious institutions commissioning liturgical furniture. The firm has reproduced vintage moldings for historic restorations and fabricated curved pergola components for exterior projects.

