UPDATE companies SET description='Flat-To-Form Metal Specialties, Inc. is a sheet metal fabrication shop based in Fremont, Michigan, founded in 1995. The company operates from a facility at 9577 W. 40th Street in Newaygo County and serves manufacturers throughout Michigan and beyond.

The shop provides a range of custom fabrication services including turret punching (24 gauge to 7 gauge), shearing, forming, laser cutting, plasma cutting, tapping, press-in fastener installation, and welding (MIG, TIG, spot, and stud). It also offers assembly of components such as hinges, fasteners, foam gaskets, locks, and clasps, as well as custom prototyping for testing before full production. The company handles jobs from a few punched holes to orders of thousands of assembled pieces.

Its customer base spans diverse manufacturing sectors. Notable clients include Mighty Lube Systematic Lubrication, Inc. in Fremont and OPCO Lubrication Systems, Inc. in West Michigan, both of which rely on Flat-To-Form for complex sheet metal parts requiring punching, forming, welding, and assembly. The company has also produced parts for office furniture and gas pump manufacturers, indicating a broad industrial reach.

Flat-To-Form emphasizes a quality management system certified to ISO 9001:2015, maintained through internal audits, management reviews, and annual surveillance audits. It differentiates itself with in-house prototyping, flexible shipping options including delivery, UPS, FedEx, and freight, and a willingness to provide its quality policy manual upon request.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Turret punching", "Shearing", "Forming", "Laser cutting", "Plasma cutting", "Tapping", "Press-in fastener installation", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Spot welding", "Stud welding", "Assembly (hinges, fasteners, foam gaskets, locks, clasps)", "Custom prototyping", "Finishing services"], "industries": ["Lubrication systems manufacturing", "Office furniture manufacturing", "Gas pump manufacturing", "General manufacturing"], "materials": ["Stainless Steel", "Aluminum", "Cold Rolled Steel", "Galvanized Steel", "Hot Rolled Pickled & Oiled Steel", "Galvannealed Steel", "Fish Paper"], "equipment": ["Turret punch press"], "volume": "Prototype to thousands of units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system with internal audits and annual surveillance audits", "Turret punch press capacity from 24 gauge to 7 gauge", "In-house welding capabilities: MIG, TIG, spot, and stud welding", "Custom prototyping for design validation before production runs", "Delivery and flexible shipping arrangements (UPS, FedEx, freight, local pickup)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1995 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Fremont, MI -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /about-us", "Turret punch press 24 gauge to 7 gauge -> /services", "Welding techniques MIG, TIG, spot, stud -> /services", "Materials: stainless steel, aluminum, cold rolled steel, galvanized, hot rolled pickled & oiled, galvannealed, fish paper -> /services", "Customers: Mighty Lube Systematic Lubrication, Inc., OPCO Lubrication Systems, Inc. -> /", "Industries: lubrication systems, office furniture, gas pumps -> /about-us", "Delivery and shipping services -> /about-us", "Custom prototyping -> /services", "Assembly services -> /services", "Laser and plasma cutting -> /services", "Press-in fasteners -> /services", "Facility address 9577 W. 40th Street, Fremont, MI 49412 -> /", "Company type: sheet metal fabrication -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Flat-To-Form Metal Specialties, Inc is a sheet metal fabrication business located in Fremont, Michigan since 1995.", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='flat-to-form-metal-specialties-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in the fall of 2006 in Gentry, Arkansas, Flint Creek Woodworks began as a cabinet door shop before expanding into a full-line custom cabinetry manufacturer.

The company designs, manufactures, and installs custom cabinets for kitchens, bathrooms, home offices, and whole-home projects. Its manufacturing facility employs advanced CNC technology to produce all-wood cabinetry featuring fully captured dado joinery, screwed-together box construction, 1/2-inch drawer bottoms, and soft-close hardware. A proprietary DuraSmooth™ finishing system is applied in-house, delivering a durable, premium surface that comes standard on every piece.

Flint Creek serves a mix of large-scale contractors, remodeling professionals, and individual homeowners across residential construction and renovation markets. The firm handles projects from initial design conception through final installation, using its own installation crews rather than subcontractors.

