UPDATE companies SET description='Florida Metal Works operates from Gulf Breeze, Florida, where it was founded in 2013 by Shane Kahl. A veteran of the U.S. Air Force with seven years of service and multiple deployments, Kahl applied the metal fabrication skills he developed in the military to launch the shop as a veteran-owned business.

The company provides custom metal fabrication and large-scale production runs for both consumer and industrial clients. Its capabilities include CNC 6 kW laser cutting, a 7-axis 150-ton CNC brake, MIG, TIG, and robotic welding, as well as fiber laser engraving for part marking and panel layouts. Work is programmed through CAD software and covers plate and sheet metals, with aluminum frequently used for railings, handrails, brackets, cabinets, and vehicle accessories.

The shop’s own product line includes items such as Sea-Doo fishfinder mounts, Ford Super Duty cowl mounting brackets, tool and battery holders, and aluminum crawfish paddles, while custom projects address specialized brackets, enclosures, and structural components for industrial buyers.

Kahl’s military background drives a focus on precision and deadline adherence, and the company emphasizes close collaboration with clients to translate requirements into finished parts.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom Fabrication", "Large-Scale Production", "CNC Laser Cutting", "CNC Braking", "MIG Welding", "TIG Welding", "Robotic Welding", "Fiber Laser Engraving", "CAD Design", "Consumer Product Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Consumer", "Industrial", "Residential", "Commercial", "Marine", "Automotive"], "materials": ["Plate Metal", "Sheet Metal", "Aluminum"], "equipment": ["CNC 6KW Laser Cutting Machine", "7-Axis 150-Ton CNC Brake", "Robotic Welding System", "CAD Software"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Veteran-owned and operated", "Founded in 2013 by Air Force veteran Shane Kahl", "In-house CNC 6 kW laser cutting and 7-axis 150-ton brake", "Robotic welding and fiber laser engraving capabilities", "Serves both consumer direct and industrial production runs"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2013 -> /about", "Veteran-owned -> /about", "Founder Shane Kahl, Air Force veteran -> /about", "Location Gulf Breeze, FL -> /about and /", "CNC 6KW laser cutting -> /", "7-axis 150-ton CNC brake -> /", "MIG, TIG, robotic welding -> /", "Fiber laser engraving -> /", "CAD software for design -> /", "Consumer and industrial clients -> /", "Residential and commercial use -> /about", "Products: brackets, cabinets, vehicle accessories, handrails -> /about", "Sea-Doo mount, Ford Super Duty brackets -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a veteran owned metal fabrication shop.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Veteran-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='florida-metal-works-gulf-breeze' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Florida Woodworks Inc. was founded in 2007 in Port St. Lucie, Florida, by Zach Hendricks, who continues to own and operate the company. Hendricks established the business to provide custom cabinetry and woodworking services tailored to individual client visions.

The company designs, builds, and installs custom kitchen and bathroom cabinetry, closet organizers, built-in units, and freestanding furniture such as desks, tables, and beds. All pieces are fabricated from scratch using premium, locally sourced American-made wood, with custom sizing and finish options. The shop serves both residential and commercial projects, handling everything from initial design through final installation.

Florida Woodworks works with homeowners, contractors, and business owners across the Treasure Coast and Palm Beach County, including Port St. Lucie, West Palm Beach, Boca Raton, Stuart, and Fort Pierce. Projects range from kitchen remodels and bathroom vanities to office built-ins and custom furniture for living spaces.

The firm emphasizes meticulous craftsmanship, personalized service, and American-made quality as its core differentiators. Hendricks stresses building client relationships to translate visions into precise, durable products, and the company offers free estimates to ensure transparency from the start.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry design and fabrication", "Kitchen cabinet installation", "Bathroom cabinet installation", "Closet organizer installation", "Custom built-in fabrication", "Custom furniture making", "Custom trim work", "Cabinet construction", "Custom sizing and finishing", "Residential and commercial project management"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial"], "materials": ["Wood", "American-made wood", "Locally sourced wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Meticulous craftsmanship with attention to every detail", "Fully customized sizing, colors, and designs", "American-made materials sourced locally", "Owner-operated personalized service since 2007", "Free, no-obligation estimates"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2007 -> db", "Owned and operated by Zach Hendricks -> db", "Headquarters in Port St. Lucie, Florida -> db", "Custom cabinetry and furniture since 2007 -> /about-us", "Services: kitchen cabinetry, bathroom cabinetry, closet organizers, custom built-ins, custom furniture -> /", "American-made, locally sourced materials -> /about-us", "Serves residential and commercial clients -> /about-us", "Areas served: Port St. Lucie, West Palm Beach, Boca Raton, etc. -> /about-us", "Free estimates offered -> /", "Emphasis on craftsmanship, personalized service, American-made quality -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We specialize in custom kitchen cabinetry, ensuring that every piece fits perfectly and complements your home''s style.", "founded_year": "2007", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='florida-woodworks-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The Food Bank of Delaware operates from its headquarters in Newark and a branch in Milford, Delaware. Founded approximately 45 years ago in a church basement, the organization has grown into a statewide network of more than 600 partner agencies.

The food bank distributes millions of pounds of food annually—including pantry staples and fresh produce from its own farms—through partner pantries, mobile pantries, school backpack programs, and direct senior deliveries. Beyond food distribution, it runs free accelerated job-training programs in warehousing/logistics and food service, and provides nutrition education, financial coaching, SNAP outreach, and legislative advocacy. The organization also operates cafes that serve the public while supporting culinary students.

Services reach food-insecure Delawareans—an estimated one in seven residents—along with adults seeking workforce credentials, seniors, children, and families. Businesses, government agencies, and other nonprofits engage as volunteers, donors, and advocacy allies.

The food bank was established to inspire hope by providing nourishment while collaborating on long-term solutions to hunger and poverty. Its stated values—compassion, respect, collaboration, empowerment, and innovation—drive a model that aims to move beyond temporary relief toward lasting financial stability for the people it serves.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Food distribution", "Warehousing and logistics job training", "Food service job training", "Nutrition education", "Financial coaching", "SNAP outreach and enrollment assistance", "Legislative advocacy", "Mobile pantry operation", "School backpack meal program", "Senior meal delivery", "Cafe and culinary student support", "Farm-based fresh produce production", "Partner agency network management", "Community food access programs"], "industries": ["Food banking and hunger relief", "Nonprofit social services", "Workforce development", "Nutrition education and counseling", "Community and economic development", "Public policy advocacy"], "materials": ["Food products", "Fresh produce", "Pantry staples"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Millions of pounds of food annually", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Grown from a church basement to a network of 600+ partners statewide over 45 years", "Distributes millions of pounds annually, including fresh produce from its own farms", "Free accelerated job training in warehousing/logistics and food service", "Mobile pantries, school backpack programs, and senior doorstep delivery", "Integrates workforce training, financial coaching, and benefits outreach to address root causes of poverty"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Newark, DE and branch in Milford, DE -> /about page", "Founded ~45 years ago from church basement -> /about page", "Network of over 600 partners statewide -> /about page", "Distributes millions of pounds of food annually -> /about page", "Fresh produce from own farms -> /about page", "Free accelerated job training in warehousing/logistics and food service -> /about page and db capabilities", "Nutrition education, financial coaching, SNAP outreach, legislative advocacy -> /about page", "Mobile pantries, school backpack programs, senior deliveries -> /about page", "Cafes supporting culinary students -> / homepage", "1 in 7 Delawareans food insecure -> / homepage", "President/CEO Cathy Kanefsky -> / homepage", "Mission and values (compassion, respect, collaboration, empowerment, innovation) -> /about page"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "The Food Bank of Delaware distributes food statewide through a network of partners.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-bank-of-delaware' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Physics was established in 2012 in Boise, Idaho, with a second base in Chelmsford, Essex, UK. The company was founded by Kalen McKenzie, who serves as partner and CEO, to identify and maximize the potential of pulsed electric field (PEF) technology in food and beverage processing.

The company acts as the sole North American, UK, and Irish provider of PEF systems designed and built by its German partner Elea. Food Physics customizes these systems — including the Belt Advantage for solid foods, Pipe Advantage for liquids, and a PEF Pilot unit for R&D — and operates pilot halls in the United States, United Kingdom, and Germany for client-specific testing. More than 100 PEF systems have been installed worldwide, and the firm holds 17 pending PEF-related patents.

Food Physics serves food manufacturers, beverage producers, and research institutions. Its technology has been applied to potato chip and french fry production, vegetable and fruit processing, freeze drying, winemaking, and the extraction of natural dyes from spirulina (the Bequia Blue project). The company works with businesses of all sizes, from pilot-scale trials to full production lines.

The firm’s stated mission is to deliver systems that increase yield, improve product stability, and reduce waste. It differentiates itself through direct access to Elea’s R&D team, on-site engineering support, a spare-parts dispatch service, and collaborative R&D projects that drive new commercial applications.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Pulsed Electric Field (PEF) system supply and customization", "Pilot-scale PEF testing", "R&D for new PEF applications", "Spare parts supply and dispatch", "Field service and maintenance", "On-site installation and training", "PEF processing for solid foods (Belt Advantage)", "PEF processing for liquid foods (Pipe Advantage)", "Freeze drying enhancement", "Potato and vegetable processing", "French fry production optimization", "Winemaking process improvement", "Natural dye extraction (spirulina)"], "industries": ["Food manufacturing", "Beverage manufacturing", "Food research and development", "Potato processing", "Vegetable and fruit processing", "Freeze drying", "French fry production", "Winemaking", "Natural dye extraction"], "materials": ["Potatoes", "Vegetables", "Fruits", "Liquid foods", "Spirulina", "Food raw materials"], "equipment": ["Elea PEF systems", "Belt Advantage", "Pipe Advantage", "PEF Pilot", "Pilot hall facilities (USA, UK, Germany)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Sole provider of Elea PEF systems in North America, UK, and Ireland", "Over 100 PEF systems installed globally", "17 PEF-related patents pending", "Pilot hall facilities in USA, UK, and Germany for custom testing", "Spare-parts dispatch for rapid service"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2012 -> /about-us", "Headquarters Boise, Idaho and Chelmsford, Essex -> /about-us", "Partnership with Elea (German manufacturer) -> /", "Sole provider of Elea PEF systems in North America, UK, Ireland -> /", "Over 100 PEF systems installed globally -> /", "17 PEF-related patents pending -> /", "Pilot hall facilities in USA, UK, Germany -> /", "Team members: Kalen McKenzie (Partner/CEO), Riley Gomez (Operations Manager), David Lethcoe (Field Service Manager), Rylan McKenzie (Finance Manager), Rose Saxton (Applications Technician) -> /about-us", "PEF systems: Belt Advantage, Pipe Advantage, PEF Pilot -> /", "Applications: potato chips, freeze drying, french fries, veggie processing -> /", "Projects: winemaking, Bequia Blue (spirulina dye), PEF-Dried -> /about-us", "Spare-parts dispatch -> /", "Field service and on-site support -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are sole provider of our Elea Pulsed Electric Field Systems (PEF) to the food, beverage and scientific sectors in North America, United Kingdom and Ireland.", "founded_year": "2012", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/food-physics-ltd/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-physics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Process Systems was founded in 1989 in Lodi, Wisconsin, and has been designing and manufacturing food processing equipment for over three decades. The company is veteran-owned and operated; in June 2025 it was acquired by Viper Engineering & Manufacturing LLC, a firm founded by Air Force veteran Brian J. Gilbertson. All operations continue at the original Lodi facility under the Food Process Systems name.

It also supplies original replacement parts, with a minimum parts order of $200, and provides a full range of services including 24/7 repair, preventative maintenance, installation and commissioning, equipment audits, retrofits, upgrades, and operator training.

Food Process Systems serves food processors worldwide across poultry, seafood, meat, dairy, snack, packaging, cereal, pet food, produce, dry goods, baked goods, candy, and frozen applications. Its equipment is designed to improve productivity, sanitation, and worker safety in processing plants.

