 million gallons -> /", "Seven employees -> /", "Virginia Department of Health Excellence in Operations awards (five categories) -> /", "Second oldest high-rate plant in Virginia -> /", "Water source: North Fork Shenandoah River -> /", "Treatment steps: disinfection, coagulation, flocculation, sedimentation, filtration -> /", "Certified operators, on-site laboratory testing -> /", "Customers include Pilgrim''s Pride, Cargill, Towns of Broadway and Timberville -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "The plant incorporates the Roberts Filter Manhattan Process of High Rate filtration. Four mixed media filters produce the finished product at a rate of 1,360 gallons per minute.", "founded_year": "1946", "employee_count": "7", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='food-processors-water-co-op' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Food Service Specialties was founded in 1985 in Columbus, Wisconsin, by lifelong friends Don Leick and Steve Lineer. The pair started the business after a prospective customer asked them to match and scale up a custom pizza sauce to ensure batch-to-batch consistency. The company remains family-owned, with the next generation now active in management.

The company formulates, manufactures, and packages tomato- and dairy-based sauces for foodservice, frozen-food, and retail customers.

